    "created_at": "2020-04-14T11:59:21Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-04-14T11:59:21Z",
    "body": "Whenever we set [[CanBlock]] to false in the web platform the reason is that the agent runs performance-critical code (e.g., a worklet might be responsible for audio processing). As I understand it `cleanupSome` effectively blocks, which would not be acceptable for any such agent. Are there scenarios where an agent with [[CanBlock]] set to true might nevertheless want to disable `cleanupSome`?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
